        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-code-traceability-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Charnia masoni apical Turing wavelength at 140 µm (565 Ma) — Model fidelity to source: 88/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The committed script integrates Schnakenberg kinetics, the Turing Jacobian, k_c^2 = (D_v f_u + D_u g_v)/(2 D_u D_v), and σ(k) as the larger eigenvalue. Euler growth on 12 wavenumbers matches the eigenvalue formula (r = 0.9984, RMSE = 0.0201). Du = Dv yields σ_max = -0.900 and is drawn as a branch-free oval. The reduction is a 1D apical row plus a chevron chart, not a curved-tissue PDE, so this is not a full 2D saturation study." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-model-fidelity-3> ;
    pk:hasScore 8.8e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-morphometric-validation> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Charnia masoni apical Turing wavelength at 140 µm (565 Ma) — Morphometric validation: 86/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Fastest-mode λ_m = 167.44 µm against the determinant-critical reference 140.4 µm (they differ because the run is above onset). Cast-versus-render orientation histograms have L1 = 0.283 and KS = 0.093. Slab occupancy profiles correlate at r = 0.800. Structure-tensor coherency is 0.456 on the cast and 0.380 on the render. No population of specimens and no direct 140 µm measurement on the fossil are claimed." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
