<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Charnia masoni apical Turing wavelength at 140 µm (565 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 87.5/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 2 scores the committed portrait chevron render of Charnia masoni at the 140.4 µm determinant-critical wavelength (565 Ma). Euler σ(k) matches the analytic dispersion at Pearson r 0.9984. The fastest mode is 167.44 µm. The diffusivity sweep matches at r 1.000 (RMSE 3.26 µm). Canonical image similarity of the 12-frame GIF against the Tübingen cast is 89.5. Equal diffusion suppresses the pattern (σ_max -0.900). Overall 87.5/100 (faithfulness 86.4, reproducibility 90.1); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 96a891cfffcbf7fb81617c1df76c424d1d7359a5; environment: python 3.12.3, numpy 2.5.4, matplotlib 3.11.2, Pillow 13.0.0, scipy 1.18.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 88, Morphological realism / specimen match 84, Parameter expressivity 90, Morphometric validation 86, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 88, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 96a891cfffcbf7fb81617c1df76c424d1d7359a5, image/png, 342160 B, 1452×902 px, artifact_sha256 261c01363f55e4ae43842c71f63a8434b2a73871e2505f7fc2e184c95023d7ec (sha256 261c01363f55e4ae43842c71f63a8434b2a73871e2505f7fc2e184c95023d7ec), spec_fingerprint 571668419f3b61d8829b66959046ef157ab530e8516cc89e6ab7b1925a5766c7. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 571668419f3b61d8829b66959046ef157ab530e8516cc89e6ab7b1925a5766c7; artifact_sha256: 261c01363f55e4ae43842c71f63a8434b2a73871e2505f7fc2e184c95023d7ec; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/README.md=4488c865883388ab..., datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_specimen.jpg=c7e8d470af175675..., datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=262080091420a03a..., datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=f4cb4c63fbfbc0fd..., datasets/charnia_masoni_turing_wavelength_s0/scout_manifest.json=ee8179dfab5e793f...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-27-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-audit. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing 1952: diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg 1979: the a - u + u^2 v kinetics integrated here. | Ford 1958 named Charnia masoni. Antcliffe and Brasier 2007 and Brasier, Antcliffe and Liu 2012 describe glide reflection rather than a sea-pen bilateral body. Dunn et al. 2021 argue for apical growth and a stem-eumetazoan affinity. Hoyal Cuthill and Conway Morris 2014 quantify fractal branching.; reconstructed_in_script: Parameters (a, b, D_u, D_v) = (0.14, 0.93, 0.062, 1.35). The determinant-critical wavelength is scaled to 1.404e-4 m. Above onset the fastest mode is longer: analytic λ_m = 167.44 µm. | Explicit-Euler σ(k) versus the eigenvalue formula (Pearson r = 0.9984, RMSE = 0.020). Equal diffusivities give σ_max = -0.900. Scaling both diffusivities moves λ with Pearson r = 1.000 and RMSE 3.26 µm. | A portrait chevron at 58°, the maximum of a four-angle CV probe (48°→87.0, 58°→89.5, 68°→84.5, 78°→83.6). Vertical gradient fraction versus commanded angle has Pearson r = 0.995.; transfer_boundary: The cast is a centimetre-scale relief frond. The chemical wavelength is 140 µm. Only outline, orientation and a stylized chevron cross that gap. The photograph does not resolve 140 µm. | Cohort words 'pigment stripe' and 'ocellus' name the Turing pattern class. The fossil is not evidence of pigment or eyes.; does_not_claim: Does not claim Ediacaran tissue ran these kinetics, or that 140.4 µm was measured on the holotype. | Does not claim a pre-565 Ma chronospecies or a Cambrian successor. The wavenumber ratio to the 6.322 mm organ-scale sibling is 45.03, which is a scale comparison, not a copied parameter set. | Does not generate the higher-order fractal branching of Hoyal Cuthill and Conway Morris 2014. One wavelength is embedded as chevrons. | Nanopublications were not signed. No profile exists at ~/.nanopub/profile.yml.." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
    pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk:hasScore 8.75e-01 ;
    pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-charnia-masoni-turing-wavelength-s0-parameter-expressivity> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Charnia masoni apical Turing wavelength at 140 µm (565 Ma) — Parameter expressivity: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Scaling D_u and D_v together by {0.35, 0.6, 1, 1.7, 2.8, 4.5} moves the fastest-mode wavelength on a 1:1 line (Pearson r = 1.000, RMSE 3.26 µm). Commanded chevron angle from 15° to 85° moves the vertical share of Sobel energy monotonically (Pearson r = 0.995). The operating angle is an interior point of the CV probe, not the edge of the search." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
